Title: Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks
URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Malkmus_and_the_Jicks
Content: Jump to content

From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia

American rock band

|     |     |
| --- | --- |
| ! | This article **needs additional citations for verification**. Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced

**********Extracted claims**********

Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks is an American rock band.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks originated in Portland, Oregon, U.S.
The genre of Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks is indie rock.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks have been active from 2000 to the present.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks are signed to Matador Records, Arts & Crafts, and Domino Recording Company.
The current members of Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks are Stephen Malkmus, Joanna Bolme, Mike Clark, and Jake Morris.
Past members of Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks include John Moen, Janet Weiss, and Joe Plummer.
Stephen Malkmus is the main singer and songwriter for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks.
Stephen Malkmus was the main singer and songwriter behind the 1990s indie rock band Pavement.
The Jicks formed in 2000.
The Jicks formed immediately after Pavement's 1999 hiatus began.
The group's first record was titled *Stephen Malkmus*.
*Stephen Malkmus* was released by Matador Records on February 13, 2001.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks made their official live debut at New York's Bowery Ballroom a few weeks before their first record was released.
Bob Nastanovich, Pavement's auxiliary percussionist, began acting as The Jicks' tour manager around the time of their live debut.
Mike Clark joined Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks on keyboards around the time of their live debut.
The band's second record, *Pig Lib*, was released in 2003.
*Pig Lib* received positive reviews, including 4/5 stars from *Rolling Stone* and an 8.0/10 from *Pitchfork Media*.
In 2003, Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks opened for Radiohead on their North American tour.
In 2004, Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks helped curate an edition of the British All Tomorrow's Parties festival.
The band released *Face the Truth* in 2005.
*Face the Truth* was released to widely positive reviews.
Most of *Face the Truth* was recorded by Stephen Malkmus alone in his basement.
Each member of the Jicks plays on at least one song on the record *Face the Truth*.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks toured minimally for *Face the Truth*.
Joe Plummer briefly filled in on drums during the *Face the Truth* touring period.
On October 2, 2006, it was reported by *Pitchfork* that John Moen had become a full-time member of The Decemberists.
John Moen was replaced by Janet Weiss as drummer for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks.
Janet Weiss was the drummer of Quasi and the then-defunct Sleater-Kinney.
The band's fourth studio album, *Real Emotional Trash*, was recorded at SnowGhost Music in Whitefish, Montana.
*Real Emotional Trash* was released on March 4, 2008.
*Real Emotional Trash* received generally positive reviews.
The band completed recording on their fifth album, *Mirror Traffic*, with Beck.
Janet Weiss's departure from the Jicks lineup was announced prior to the release of *Mirror Traffic*.
Jake Morris, ex-Joggers drummer, took Janet Weiss's place.
The band's sixth studio album, *Wig Out at Jagbags*, was released on January 7, 2014.
*Wig Out at Jagbags* was recorded in the La Chapelle studio in Belgium.
Pavement's F.O.H. live sound engineer, Remko 'El Duche' Schouten, was involved in the recording of *Wig Out at Jagbags*.
Overdubs for *Wig Out at Jagbags* were done in Berlin.
Stephen Malkmus lived in Berlin from 2012 until 2014.
*Wig Out at Jagbags* was mixed in Amsterdam's IJland Studio.
On March 26, 2018, it was announced that the band's seventh studio album, *Sparkle Hard*, would be released.
*Sparkle Hard* was released on May 18, 2018.
Since about 2012, Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks have shown a greater willingness to occasionally play Pavement songs.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks generally play one or two Pavement songs per show.
Commonly played Pavement songs in later Jicks performances have included "In the Mouth a Desert", "Shady Lane", "Box Elder", and "Stereo".
Stephen Malkmus has been the vocalist and guitarist for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2000 to the present.
Joanna Bolme has been the bassist, vocalist, and synthesizer player for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2000 to the present.
Mike Clark has been the keyboardist, synthesizer player, and guitarist for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2001 to the present.
Jake Morris has been the drummer for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2011 to the present.
John Moen was the drummer, percussionist, and vocalist for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2000–2005 and 2005–2006.
Joe Plummer was the drummer for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks in 2005.
Janet Weiss was the drummer for Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks from 2006–2011.
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks' studio albums include *Stephen Malkmus* (2001), *Pig Lib* (2003), *Face the Truth* (2005), *Real Emotional Trash* (2008), *Mirror Traffic* (2011), *Wig Out at Jagbags* (2014), and *Sparkle Hard* (2018).
Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks have released singles including "Phantasies" (2001), "Discretion Grove" (2001), "Jenny & the Ess-Dog" (2001), "Jo Jo's Jacket" (2001), "Dark Wave" (2003), "Baby C'mon" (2005), "Kindling for the Master" (2006), "Baltimore" (2008), "Gardenia" (2008), "Cold Son" (2008), "Tigers" (2011), "Senator" (2011), "Stick Figures in Love" (2012), "Gorgeous Georgie" b/w "Wheels of Fire" (2012), "Lariat" (2013), "Middle America" (2018), "Shiggy" (2018), and "Refute" (2018).

