Title: One True King
URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_True_King
Content: Jump to content

From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia

Content organization based in Austin, Texas

This article is about the gaming organization. For the novel by Soman Chainani, see One True King (novel) "One True King (novel)").

| ! |
| Full name | O

**********Extracted claims**********

OTK Media, Inc. does business as One True King.
One True King is an American media organization.
One True King is based in Austin, Texas.
One True King was founded on October 11, 2020.
One True King was founded by content creators Asmongold, Mizkif, Esfand, Rich Campbell, and Tips Out.
The organization's stated purpose was to build an organization around friends and friendship.
One True King has been described by its members as a media production company and lifestyle brand.
One True King is not confined to any one game or section on Twitch.
One True King has gained notability for not receiving major backing from corporations.
One True King primarily focuses on online content creation.
One True King has previously competed professionally in World of Warcraft.
One True King has been subject to multiple controversies surrounding racism and sexual assault involving its members and founders since its founding.
One True King's Twitch channel has 315,345 followers as of April 30, 2025.
One True King's main YouTube channel has 605,000 subscribers as of April 30, 2025.
One True King's main YouTube channel has 41.4 million views as of April 30, 2025.
One True King unveiled its professional World of Warcraft roster alongside its initial announcement.
The original World of Warcraft roster consisted of Trill, Mes, Cdew, and Samiyam.
One True King's World of Warcraft team competed at Blizzard-sanctioned events for one season during the Shadowlands expansion.
One True King announced a partnership with Artesian Builds.
Artesian Builds is a pre-built PC company.
On October 27, 2020, One True King announced the addition of Nick Polom, also known as Nmplol.
Nmplol joined One True King as a content creator and co-owner.
In December 2020, One True King partnered with Complexity Gaming's World of Warcraft team.
The partnership involved providing coverage of the game's Race to World First event.
One True King held daily roundtable discussions about the Race to World First event.
On October 11, 2021, One True King announced that Cyr would be joining the organization as a content creator.
On November 21, 2021, One True King announced that Tectone would be joining the organization as a content creator.
On January 2, 2022, One True King announced that Emiru would be joining the organization.
On March 2, 2022, One True King parted ways with Artesian Builds.
The parting ways with Artesian Builds followed a giveaway controversy involving Artesian Builds.
One True King won the "Best Content Organization" award at The Streamer Awards on March 12, 2022.
On March 27, 2022, One True King announced that BruceDropEmOff would be joining the organization as a content creator.
On July 21, 2022, One True King announced that Sodapoppin would be joining the organization as a content creator and co-owner.
On September 19, 2022, Twitch streamer Trainwreckstv accused Mizkif of downplaying and covering up an alleged sexual assault incident involving CrazySlick and AdrianahLee.
On September 19, 2022, streamer Ice Poseidon published a set of comments made by Mizkif from 2018 to 2019.
The comments made by Mizkif were characterized as racist and homophobic.
Mizkif worked with Ice Poseidon during his early streaming career.
Mizkif was placed on leave by One True King on September 20, 2022.
On December 31, 2022, One True King released a statement about the allegation of Mizkif covering up an incident of sexual assault.
A Texas-based law firm, Jackson Walker, investigated the allegation against Mizkif.
The investigation's counsel did not find direct evidence that Mizkif attempted to minimize or cover up sexual assault.
Mizkif's status as an OTK member was reinstated.
On January 2, 2023, Mizkif uploaded a video apologizing for insensitive and tone-deaf behavior displayed in an early October broadcast.
On December 16, 2022, co-owner Rich Campbell announced his resignation from the organization.
Rich Campbell's resignation was due to sexual assault allegations.
On December 23, 2022, the official OTK Twitter account announced jschlatt would be departing the organization.
Jschlatt continues as an advisor for the YouTube team.
Jschlatt has a stake in Starforge Systems.
On January 24, 2023, BruceDropEmOff left the organization.
On January 27, 2023, BruceDropEmOff was indefinitely suspended from Twitch, citing ban evasion.
On January 31, 2023, Emiru was announced as a new co-owner of the organization.
Emiru was previously a content creator in the organization.
On January 31, 2023, ExtraEmily joined the organization as a content creator.
On February 5, 2024, One True King announced that WillNeff would be joining the organization as a content creator.
On October 16, 2024, Asmongold announced he was "stepping away" from his leadership roles at OTK and Starforge Systems.
Asmongold's announcement followed backlash over his comments on Palestinians affected by the Gaza war.
On November 1, 2024, Tectone left the organization after his three-year contract expired and he decided not to renew it.
On February 21, 2025, Asmongold announced on his stream that he had left the organization.
Current members of One True King include Esfand, Mizkif, TipsOut, Nmplol, Cyr, Emiru, Sodapoppin, and ExtraEmily.
Esfand is a co-founder, co-owner, and content creator of One True King.
Mizkif is a co-founder, co-owner, and content creator of One True King.
TipsOut is a co-founder and co-owner of One True King.
Nmplol is a co-owner and content creator of One True King.
Cyr is a content creator of One True King.
Emiru is a co-owner and content creator of One True King.
Sodapoppin is a co-owner and content creator of One True King.
ExtraEmily is a content creator of One True King.
Former members of One True King include Rich Campbell, Jschlatt, BruceDropEmOff, Tectone, Asmongold, and WillNeff.
On August 7, 2022, OTK and YouTuber Cr1TiKaL announced the founding of Starforge Systems.
Starforge Systems is a technology company focused on building computers.
Starforge Systems was met with backlash due to allegedly high prices of its products.
Starforge Systems responded by decreasing its prices by $100.
Nick Dankner is the CEO of Starforge Systems.
Nick Dankner was the COO of Artesian Builds, a defunct pre-built PC company.
In June 2022, OTK announced a partnership with WePlay Esports.
WePlay Esports is a content production company.
The partnership included the unveiling of a Los Angeles-based content studio.
The "OTK Games Expo" was the first event held under the partnership.
The "OTK Games Expo" showcased nearly 30 video games from various indie developers.
In February 2023, OTK announced the founding of Mythic Talent.
Mythic Talent is a full-service talent management company.
Mythic Talent was co-founded by OTK members Asmongold and TipsOut.
William Lucas is the CEO of Mythic Talent.
William Lucas is a veteran of esports organization Tempo Storm and the AFK Agency.
On May 17, 2023, OTK announced a partnership with GamerSupps.
GamerSupps is an energy drink company.
GamerSupps is owned by former OTK member Jschlatt.
On June 12, 2023, OTK announced the launch of game publishing company Mad Mushroom during the OTK Games Expo.
On August 10, 2023, Mad Mushroom announced the appointment of Mike Silbowitz as its CEO.
OTK Schooled is a quiz game show.
OTK Schooled was created and hosted by Twitch streamer and OTK member Mizkif.
OTK Schooled is produced by One True King.
OTK Schooled tests the knowledge of its contestants with school-related questions.
OTK Schooled is frequently compared to the American gameshow franchise Are You Smarter than a 5th Grader?.
OTK Schooled gained popularity because of several cheating controversies that happened during the show.
OTK Game Day is a weekly sports show.
OTK Game Day is hosted by Twitch streamer and OTK member Nmplol and One True King.
In OTK Game Day, OTK members go up against other streamers in various physical team-based sports.
On November 9, 2021, Mizkif and One True King announced a new game show called OTK Parasocial.
OTK Parasocial appears to be in the style of Family Feud.
Family Feud is an American television game show.
OTK Parasocial prompts players to “guess the most popular answers to questions.”
In January 2021, One True King's World of Warcraft team participated in the first edition of the Shadowlands Arena World Championship.
One True King's World of Warcraft team finished 3rd among North American teams in the Shadowlands Arena World Championship.
At Cup 2, One True King's World of Warcraft team made it to the finals of the North American bracket.
One True King lost to Kawhi 1–4 at Cup 2.
At Cup 3, One True King's World of Warcraft team made it to the semi-finals.
One True King lost to Cloud9 0–3 at Cup 3.
At the fourth and final cup of season one, One True King's World of Warcraft team made it to the quarterfinals.
One True King lost to Charlotte Phoenix 1–3 at the fourth and final cup.
One True King's World of Warcraft team finished second in the standings with 300 points.
One True King's World of Warcraft team qualified for the Regional Circuit Championships.
One True King finished the circuit with 8 points.
One True King tied for the 3rd place spot in North America with Golden Guardians.
One True King advanced to the Arena World Championship Season 1 Finals.
One True King made it to the semi-finals in the Arena World Championship Season 1 Finals.
One True King lost to Cloud9 in the semi-finals of the Arena World Championship Season 1 Finals.
One True King finished the season in 3rd place.
On June 11, 2021, Cdew announced via Twitter that One True King decided not to renew the team's contracts for the upcoming expansion.
One True King has held several charity streams.
The charity streams benefited the non-profit organization Games for Love.
One True King's first charity stream took place on November 23, 2020.
Over $250,000 was raised during the first charity stream through opening rare Pokémon cards.
The first charity stream averaged 70,000 viewers.
A second charity stream for Games for Love took place on March 22, 2021.
The second charity stream raised $600,000.
One True King's third charity stream took place over two days from June 22–23, 2021.
The third charity stream raised $593,597.
In March 2022, One True King held two charity streams benefiting relief efforts for those affected by the 2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine.
These charity streams raised over $500,000.
On April 29, 2023, One True King and OTK member Esfand organized a charity event called Charity Lift-A-Thon.
Charity Lift-A-Thon featured OTK members and other Twitch streamers lifting weights for charity.
Charity Lift-A-Thon had a goal of lifting one pound for every dollar donated.
Charity Lift-A-Thon raised more than $140,601 towards Games for Love.
One True King was nominated for Content Group of the Year at the Esports Awards in 2022.
One True King was nominated for Esports Content Creator of the Year at the Esports Awards in 2023.
One True King won "Best Content Organization" at The Streamer Awards in 2021.
One True King was nominated for "Best Content Organization" at The Streamer Awards in 2022.
One True King was nominated for "Best Content Organization" at The Streamer Awards in 2023.
One True King was nominated for "Best Content Organization" at The Streamer Awards in 2024.

