The Great Northern War was fought between a coalition of Denmark–Norway, Russia, and Saxony-Poland on one side and Sweden on the other side.
Norwegians were tired of the war by 1720.
The Norwegian Army had been weakened in early 1716 by the withdrawal of 5000 of its best troops to support Denmark's defense.

