**********Extracted claims**********

"By the Way, I Forgive You" is Brandi Carlile's sixth studio album.
The album "By the Way, I Forgive You" was released on February 16, 2018.
The album was recorded at RCA Studio A in Nashville, Tennessee.
The album's genres include Americana, symphonic pop, and rock.
The album has a total length of 43 minutes and 25 seconds.
The labels for the album are Low Country Sound and Elektra.
Dave Cobb and Shooter Jennings co-produced the album.
Brandi Carlile's album "The Firewatcher's Daughter" was released in 2015, preceding "By the Way, I Forgive You".
Brandi Carlile's album "In These Silent Days" was released in 2021, following "By the Way, I Forgive You".
"The Joke" was released as the lead single from "By the Way, I Forgive You".
"Party of One" was released as a single from "By the Way, I Forgive You".
The album art for "By the Way, I Forgive You" is an original painting by Scott Avett.
"By the Way, I Forgive You" won a Grammy Award for Best Americana Album in 2019.
"By the Way, I Forgive You" was nominated for Album of the Year at the Grammy Awards.
"The Joke" was released on November 13, 2017.
The official music video for "The Joke" was released on February 16, 2018.
Former U.S. President Barack Obama named "The Joke" as one of his favorite songs of 2017.
"The Joke" reached number 4 on the Adult Alternative Songs chart.
"The Joke" reached number 43 on the Hot Rock Songs chart.
A remix of "Party of One" featuring English singer-songwriter Sam Smith was released as the second single on October 17, 2018.
A portion of the profits from the song "Party of One" featuring Sam Smith was designated to benefit Children In Conflict.
"Party of One" reached number 29 on the Adult Contemporary radio chart.
A music video of the album version of "Party of One" starring Elisabeth Moss was released in December 2018.
Brandi Carlile performed "The Joke" on "Jimmy Kimmel Live!" in January 2018.
Brandi Carlile performed "The Joke" and "Whatever You Do" on "The Late Show with Stephen Colbert" in April 2018.
Brandi Carlile performed "The Joke" on "The Howard Stern Show" in April 2018.
Brandi Carlile performed "Hold Out Your Hand" on "Full Frontal with Samantha Bee" in August 2018.
The song "The Mother" commemorates Brandi Carlile's daughter.
The song "Fulton County Jane Doe" is based on the real-life story of an unidentified murder victim in Fulton County, Georgia.
"By the Way, I Forgive You" received positive reviews from music critics.
The album "By the Way, I Forgive You" has an average score of 81 out of 100 on Metacritic.
The Metacritic score of 81 out of 100 for the album indicates "Universal acclaim."
"Rolling Stone" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 12th best album of 2018.
NPR rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 19th best album of 2018.
Thrillist rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 36th best album of 2018.
"Vice" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 22nd best album of 2018.
"PopMatters" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 63rd best album of 2018.
Refinery29 rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 9th best album of 2018.
"Entertainment Weekly" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 11th best album of 2018.
Chris Willman of "Variety" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 2nd best album of 2018.
Kevin Coffey of the "Omaha World-Herald" rated "By the Way, I Forgive You" as the 2nd best album of 2018.
Brandi Carlile was nominated for Artist of the Year at the 2018 Americana Music Honors & Awards.
