From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia

German hydrogeologist

|     |     |
| --- | --- |
| ! | hide **This article has multiple issues.** Please help **improve it** or discuss these issues on the **talk page**. _( Learn how and when to r

**********Extracted claims**********

Christian Wolkersdorfer is a German hydrogeologist and mining hydrogeologist.
Christian Wolkersdorfer is known for his work in mine water management and environmental remediation.
Christian Wolkersdorfer has held academic positions across Europe, North America, and Africa.
Christian Wolkersdorfer contributed to research on water management in abandoned mines.
Christian Wolkersdorfer is a member of the South African Academy of Sciences.
Christian Wolkersdorfer is the President of the International Mine Water Association.
Christian Wolkersdorfer was born on February 17, 1964.
Christian Wolkersdorfer was born in Schwabach/Mittelfranken, Germany.
Christian Wolkersdorfer's alma mater is Clausthal University of Technology.
Christian Wolkersdorfer has two children, Karoline and Franziska.
